## Calculating Factorials Safely

### Basic Factorial

```xiom
fn factorial(n: Int) -> Int {
  let mut result = 1;
  let mut i = 2;
  while i <= n {
    result = result * i;
    i += 1;
  };
  result
}
```

### The Overflow Problem

Int has a maximum value of about 2.1 billion. 13! already exceeds this. The result wraps around to negative numbers silently — a catastrophic bug.

### Adding Contract Protection

```xiom
requires { n >= 0; }
requires { n <= 12; }
fn factorial(n: Int) -> Int {
  let mut result = 1;
  let mut i = 2;
  while i <= n {
    result = result * i;
    i += 1;
  };
  result
}
```

Now calling `factorial(13)` triggers the contract. No silent overflow.

### Factorial Table

```xiom
fn print_factorial_table(max: Int) {
  let mut i = 0;
  while i <= max {
    let f = factorial(i);
    io.println(f);
    i += 1;
  };
}
```

